  border-radius: var(--ds-tag-radius-lg, var(--ds-radius-lg));
}
.rottay-tag-shell.rottay-tag-shell--modern[data-part='root'][data-part='root'][data-radius='full'] {
  border-radius: var(--ds-tag-radius-full, 9999px);
}

/* ---- solid fill: the variant map. The bare rule carries `default`, which is the
        map's own fallback for an unrecognised variant.

        CONTRAST LAW (R0/Axe): chromatic solid fills deepen toward black until
        white ink clears WCAG AA on EVERY governed source -- the raw 500-level
        hues fail (white on rottay #22C55E = 2.28, on bithire #D6A04E = 2.33)
        and no static ink survives both light (rottay) and dark (TMM #8A6B00)
        semantic hues. The mix derives from the tenant's own resolved hue, so
        the ramp stays hue-faithful with no ramp lookup. Measured white-ink
