 * ENGINE-AGNOSTIC: TooltipContent has a single render tree (no engine split), so
 * it gets one file here rather than a per-engine pair. It is a
 * standalone `forwardRef` piece with its own arrow-positioning logic, not the
 * bubble either engine's Tooltip renders -- those carry
 * `rottay-tooltip-bubble--{modern,rustic}` and have their own skins.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's
 * base layer, so a layered rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity.
 * Unlayered outranks preflight and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPED ON `rottay-tooltip-content`, the component's own first-party classname
 * (grep-verified: only this file's component renders it). Note it is NOT matched
 * by the personality/tenant rules on `.rottay-tooltip` -- a class selector is an
 * exact match, not a prefix. The arrow hangs off the content as a child so its
 * rule cannot reach a stray `rottay-tooltip-arrow` elsewhere.
 *
 * The arrow's per-side offsets stay inline: they are layout, not paint. No
 * border is declared here, so the P-48 (0,4,0) floor does not apply. Values
 * transcribed verbatim from `compound/Content/index.tsx`.
 */

.rottay-tooltip-content {
  background-color: var(--ds-tooltip-bg, var(--ds-color-text-primary));
  color: var(--ds-tooltip-color, var(--ds-color-bg-base));
  border-radius: var(--ds-tooltip-radius, 0.375rem);
  box-shadow: var(--ds-tooltip-shadow, var(--ds-shadow-lg));
}

.rottay-tooltip-content > .rottay-tooltip-arrow {
  background-color: var(--ds-tooltip-bg, var(--ds-color-text-primary));
  transform: rotate(45deg);
}

}
@layer rottay-components {
