@layer rottay-components {
/**
 * DataTerminalCard skin — engine-agnostic, DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47).
 * Home: foundation/tokens/css/presentation/components/skin/data-terminal-card.css. The component renders
 * one DOM tree under every engine (no engines/ split), so it has a single skin
 * covering BOTH of its scope classes: `ds-data-terminal-card` (the four variant
 * bodies CommandCard/HUDCard/CircuitCard/MatrixCard, selected by `data-variant`
 * 1..4) and `ds-data-terminal-stat` (DataTerminalStat).
 *
 * DELIBERATELY UNLAYERED (P-47): every `rottay-*` layer sorts before Tailwind's
 * base layer, so a layered rule loses to preflight regardless of specificity.
 * Unlayered outranks preflight and still yields to a caller's inline `style`.
 *
 * SCOPE ROOT carries a SINGLE class (`ds-data-terminal-card` OR
 * `ds-data-terminal-stat`) — not the usual `ds-structure ds-<comp>` pair — plus
 * `data-part='root'` and the contract attributes `data-variant` (card only),
 * `data-trend`, `data-band` (card + progress-fill). Every painted node is a
 * descendant with its own `data-part`. Because there is only one root class, the
 * specificity budget below is bought from that one class plus REPEATED
 * `data-part` and/or the contract attributes — never an incidental attribute.
 *
 * SPECIFICITY (P-48): the Platform-only Rottay artifact ships an unlayered
 * `html[data-tenant]:not([data-theme]):not(.light) *` at (0,3,1) that sets
 * `border-color` on every element, and the modern/rustic Typography skins paint
 * every composed `Text` at
 * `.rottay-typography.rottay-typography--<engine>.rottay-typography--<engine>[data-color='default']`
 * = (0,4,0). Therefore, with one root class:
 *   - NON-BORDER paint on a Box/icon (background, background-image, background-size,
 *     border-radius, icon color) beats preflight at (0,3,0): one class + the
 *     descendant `data-part` repeated once (or the root class + one contract attr
 *     + the descendant part).
 *   - A BORDER COLOR must reach (0,4,0): one class + the descendant `data-part`
 *     repeated (or a contract attr) for three more units. `border: none`/width-only
 *     resets carry no color and are exempt — none exist here.
 *   - `color` on a composed `Text` must EXCEED the Typography skin's (0,4,0), so it
 *     reaches (0,5,0): one class + the descendant `data-part` repeated to four, or
 *     one class + one contract attr + the part repeated to three. (Icon color has
 *     no Typography competitor and wins at (0,3,0).)
 *
 * STATE: `getProgressColor(progress)` is a threshold bucket over static tokens and
 * is STATE-SELECTED, so it becomes rules keyed on the stamped `data-band`
 * (high -> success, mid -> warning, low -> error). `trendColor` is the binary
 * `trend === 'up' ? success : error` and becomes rules keyed on `data-trend`.
 *
 * RUNTIME HATCHES (uncounted quoted custom-property keys set inline, consumed here):
 *   - `--ds-dtc-live`  — LiveIndicator's ring colour is caller-passed (CircuitCard
 *     passes the band-derived progress colour, MatrixCard passes success). It is
 *     computed from data, so no enumerable rule holds it; the caller sets it and
 *     both rings read it.
 *   - `--ds-dtc-radius` — ProgressBar's `border-radius: height / 2` is computed from
 *     a runtime `height` prop; the track sets it and both track + fill read it.
 *
 * SAME-PART STATIC SIBLINGS: the three terminal-dots and the corner-brackets share
 * one `data-part` each with no distinguishing stamp, so they are selected by
 * scope-anchored `:nth-child` — byte-exact for these hardcoded, fixed-order
 * decorative siblings.
 *
 * Values transcribed verbatim from index.tsx (the `DS` token map + the two
